Dispatcharr is a self-hosted IPTV stream management platform that provides
intelligent stream management, EPG auto-matching, and compatibility with
popular media centers like Plex and Jellyfin.

Key Features:
- IPTV Stream Management: Proxy and manage IPTV streams with bandwidth
  optimization and failover support
- EPG Auto-Matching: AI-powered Electronic Program Guide matching using
  sentence transformers and fuzzy matching
- HDHomeRun Emulation: Compatible with Plex Live TV, Jellyfin, and other
  HDHomeRun clients for seamless integration
- M3U/XMLTV Support: Import and export M3U playlists and XMLTV EPG data
- VOD Support: Manage Video on Demand content for movies and TV series
- Real-time Statistics: Monitor stream health and performance through a
  modern web dashboard
- Smart Playlists: Filter, group, and organize streams with automatic
  failover support

The web interface is accessible on port 9191 by default. HDHomeRun
emulation is available on port 5004 for media center integration.

This port includes Django-based backend with Celery for background tasks,
Redis for caching and message queue, PostgreSQL for data storage, and
Nginx as a reverse proxy.
